4:player

280:After a night of reexamining everything, Jane and I seem to be getting nowhere. So, we decide to split up and investigate.
282:I instinctively jot down the questions that have been plaguing my mind over the past couple of days on a scrap of paper and toss it into the star-shaped glass bottle on my desk.
283:In the blink of an eye, the bottle is almost half full with the scraps of paper I've been tossing in.
284:I shake the bottle, and it glimmers under the rays of morning light. I find myself being pulled back into my memories of that distant summer day...
285:A-37
286:I asked around in the store, and they said this wish bottle works wonders. So I got one for you.
287:Why the sudden gift?
288:Because I hope your wishes will always come true.
289:After A-37 left, I would occasionally throw in small pieces of paper with random thoughts. Unfortunately, the wish bottle never made any of them come true.
290:I wonder when A-37 will return to One Han City. Actually, the employment contract between us is still active...
291:Wait!
293:I send the photo I took to A-37 without expecting much. After all, I haven't heard from A-37 in so long, so I have no idea if he would reply.
294:Unexpectedly, A-37 replies almost immediately.
295:(Text Message) This isn't what you should be focused on right now.
296:(Text Message) If you encounter anyone with that tattoo again, stay away from them.
297:With a glimmer of hope in my heart, I send a photo of the jade forgery.
298:(Text Message) It's a long story. I'm now actually a Jyanshi who works as a full-time supervisor and part-time detective...
299:(Text Message) Can you dig up information on this jade for me?
300:My phone goes silent for a long while... As disappointment starts to creep into me, finally--Ding!
301:(Text Message) It sounds like you've signed more employment contracts than I have.
302:(Text Message) That isn't the point!
303:A short while later, A-37 sends me a link that leads to a collector's trading website, and I notice the main image for one of the sold items is practically identical to the Heart of Divinity!
304:I quickly view the transaction's information. It was completed several days ago, and the seller is actually Saturne!
306:The garden remains the same, and the gentle summer breeze carries along the fragrance of flowers. Saturne slices a piece of lemon tart and hands it to me while I explain everything to him.
307:Saturne
308:Who knew that delivery guy would be the one who created the opportunity for our reunion. Haha!
309:Are you two... close?
310:Sort of. Haha! We used to be old friends, and now we're allies.
311:Let's talk about him another time and focus on the jade I sold.
312:Actually, it wasn't the Heart of Divinity. It's known as Hoarfrost. It's a great piece too, but it's no match for the Heart of Divinity.
313:However, due to its similarity with the priceless Heart of Divinity, its price was really driven up on the market.
314:Such a gorgeous piece of jade isn't the best?! Then how dazzling is the real Heart of Divinity?
315:As I let my imagination run wild, Saturne suddenly whispers rather mysteriously.
316:Actually, the Heart of Divinity's value isn't solely derived from its quality, its legend is a significant factor as well.
317:Oh... I've heard about it from Qing Luan. It was inlaid on a royal chalice in Northland and passed down for centuries.
318:Haha! As far as I know, it goes way beyond that.
319:According to legend, it is the heart of a god. The Northland Church was built atop the spot it where was found because people believe that it's the closest point to the Heart of God.
321:However, during a succession ceremony, the new pope was consumed by greed when he held the Heart of Divinity. In a moment of madness, the new pope slaughtered his predecessor and his supporters.
322:Not long after, the knight commander coveted it as well and killed the new pope for it. The church was in turmoil, and the flames of war blazed...
323:The common belief is that the red design that resembles blood vessels on the legendary Heart of Divinity was formed naturally, but as far as I know, it was formed with the blood of Northland's people.
324:Saturne looks down and takes a sip of coffee, seemingly taking a moment of silence to mourn the lives lost in that war.
325:It's like I listened to a story from that book, Church Miracles.
326:Saturne makes me some scented tea with a smile, then pushes it toward me and motions me to have a taste.
327:Indeed, it's recorded in a somewhat similar book that's kept in the possession of the Sage Astra.
328:Saturne, you seem to know a lot about Northland's church.
329:Haha! Everyone from Northland has knowledge about the church to some extent.
330:I even know many tales about the Heart of Divinity, but you're here to locate Hoarfrost's buyer, so I'll get to the point.
331:Please do tell.
333:But he was wearing clown makeup, very conspicuous.
334:!
335:Is there anything else you can tell me about him?
336:Hmm... Before leaving, he asked if I was interested in Bamboo Cloud's roast geese.
337:Such a weirdo, right?
339:Clown makeup... I think I know who it is.
341:Head to Bamboo Cloud and inform Fuuka Minami about this lead.
342:I leave Saturne's place and take a seat at the café.
343:I happen to know someone in One Han City who wears clown makeup. I may not know him that well, but it does sound like something he would do...
344:But how do I find him?
345:???
346:Boom!
347:AHHH!!!
348:Ju
349:Weren't you thinking about me and waiting for me? So, why are you so surprised?
350:Ju pulls the chair in front of me and takes a seat.
351:Let me guess... Are you considering the best way to ask me? No need to overthink it--just go ahead and ask... At the very least, I'm happy to help right now.
352:So, did you really steal the Heart of Divinity?
353:Is it wrong to add some relaxing comedy to this joyous anniversary celebration?
354:It wasn't relaxing for me at all!
355:Hahaha! That's because instead of sitting at the table and play with me, my opponents just want to catch me...
356:Why did you steal the Heart of Divinity?
357:Haha! Relax! It was just a joker's joke!
358:Those two auction house employees were discussing their theft so seriously, and they kept reassuring each other by saying it was all for Northland... Isn't that interesting?
359:Hahaha! When humans think, even the gods have their minds blown! Boom!! Like a computer system that crashes after hundreds of forms are opened! Hahahahahaha!
360:I see you're in a really good mood... So, where's the Heart of Divinity?
361:Ju raises his wrist to check the time, then tips his hat with a smile.
362:It's almost time. Go take a look at Bamboo Cloud. Oh, Happy Detective Day! Outstanding... Little! DE--TECT--TIVE!
363:I return to Bamboo Cloud as Ju suggested, and the manager leads me to a private room on the second floor.
365:Fuuka Minami
366:Oh, it's you, {var:player_nickname}. You came at just the right time. I heard you were so busy solving the case that you skipped breakfast, and that concerns me.
367:You're a guest in Bamboo Cloud, so forget about your job as the supervisor for now and enjoy the food!
368:Fuuka Minami rings the call bell.
369:Waiter
370:Welcome to the bamboo forest of deliciousness!
371:Oh, what a warm welcome...
372:If our most popular breakfast item is what you seek, then look no further than the Four Heavenly Kings!
373:I don't think I asked?
374:Steamed Spare Ribs with Garlic and Black Beans, Braised Tripe, Wonton Noodles with Chicken Feet and Egg Tarts, Shrimp Dumplings and Barbecued Pork with Red Rice Sausages...
375:Wasn't it supposed to be four...
376:Everyone knows the Four Heavenly Kings consist of twelve! If they are not to your liking, may I recommend the thirty-six Eight Vajra Kings!
377:Come on, don't be shy. What would you like to order?
378:Well... Roast goose?
379:Fuuka Minami suddenly turns ashen...
380:That dish is bad luck! Let's skip it for now. I've been thinking about taking it off the menu anyway.
381:Huh?! Why would you remove your best seller?!
382:I guess it's time I told you the truth.
383:While I was eating at Bamboo Cloud a few days ago, I found the real Heart of Divinity inside the belly of my roast goose.
384:It was then that I realized the Heart of Divinity in the auction house had been switched.
385:I didn't know who it was, or why that person did it! So, while you were investigating the theft of the fake jade, I used the opportunity to find out who was playing these tricks right under my nose. I hope you'll forgive me for that.
386:Don't worry, it's our secret. A thousand-year-old treasure that was once inlaid in a royal chalice had been stuffed into a goose's belly. It's absolutely absurd...
387:Ms. Minami, your roast goose is served.
388:Huh? I thought we didn't order one?
389:What? The kitchen said you made an additional order...
390:Heh! It's happening again. Just put it down.
391:Fuuka Minami's face visibly darkens. She opens the lid, sighs heavily, and closes it once more.
392:I curiously take a peek and see a playing card with "I Wish You Happiness" on it. I think I know who's behind this...
393:But I should keep it to myself!
394:Fuuka Minami tears the card into bits, takes a few deep breaths, and gives me her folding fan.
395:Now, it's my turn.
396:Your detective mission is over. Here's a bonus on top of your regular payment. Please take it.
398:I leave Saturne's place and arrive at Bamboo Cloud.
399:While I was eating at Bamboo Cloud a few days ago, I found the real Heart of Divinity inside the belly of my roast goose!
400:It was then that I realized the Heart of Divinity in the auction house had been switched.
401:I didn't know who it was, or why that person did it! So, while you were investigating the theft of the fake jade, I used the opportunity to find out who was playing these tricks right under my nose. I hope you'll forgive me for that.
402:It's happening again. Just put it down.
403:I curiously take a peek and see a playing card with "I Wish You Happiness" on it.
404:Clown makeup and playing cards... I think I know who's behind all of this.
405:Let me check in the kitchen!
406:Forget it, it's too late. I gave the order to hunt him down right away that day, but we couldn't capture him even after turning Bamboo Cloud upside down.
407:Fuuka Minami tears the card into bits as she speaks, takes a few deep breaths, and continues.
408:I'll deal with the rest.
409:About your compensation for this detective mission...
410:She snaps her finger and the waiter brings over an exquisite gift box.
411:I open it carefully, and to my surprise, I find Hoarfrost lying inside!
412:The are many stories about the Heart of Divinity already, so I'll leave the stories about Hoarfrost in your hands.
413:But this jade has many stories about it too...
414:Hmm? Many, you say?
415:Fuuka Minami fans herself with a smile.
416:But I think our story... has only just begun!
419:Who switched the Heart of Divinity for a forgery? Where is the real one? What was that tattoo on Toku? And what did he mean when he said the Heart of Divinity belongs to Northland?
420:After I contact Saturne, he invites me to meet him at Lotus Gardens.
421:They say its owner will gain both power and the support of the people, and so it was inlaid into a royal chalice passed down through generations of popes.
422:The buyer didn't leave his contact details. We just conducted an offline transaction at an agreed location.
425:Bamboo Cloud
426:Memento Received - Elegant Folding Fan
427:Memento Received - White Jade "Hoarfrost"
429:As the image of A-37 appears in my mind, I finally realize why Toku's tattoo had been so familiar! A-37 had a similar tattoo on his arm! It wasn't a turtle, it was the Genbu!
